error[E0945]: the judgment `⊢` needs the library `std/semantics`
 --> tests/neg/e0945_judgment_library.hgn:3:34
  |
3 | oneStep : {x y : G.node} -> tc G ⊢ G.edge x y -> tc G ⊢ path x y. (*~ E0945 *)
  |                                  ^ judgment here
  |
  = note: `P ⊢[d] r t̄` stands for `derives (programOf P) d (atom ρ [v t̄])` of `std/semantics`
  = help: add `%use "std/semantics".` to the file

error[E0960]: `(tc g).path x y` is not a type: it applies a relation to arguments
 --> tests/neg/e0945_judgment_library.hgn:5:44
  |
5 | coerced : (g : graph) -> {x y : g.node} -> (tc g).path x y -> Type. (*~ E0960 *)
  |                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an applied relation
  |
  = note: as a meta type, an applied relation would be `⇑(r t̄)`, the lift of a fact type of an application, which no object term has: the fact type of a relation `r` is `r` alone
  = note: an applied relation is a proposition of the program that owns it: a relation of an instance, a module or a functor application `(f ā).r`, or one opened from an instance; a variable's relation is read by every program over it, and a relation of the file or of the enclosing body is not owned yet
  = help: load `std/semantics` (`%use "std/semantics".`): an applied relation of `tc g` is then its judgment `tc g ⊢ r t̄`

